  "comment": "IDN / A-label canonicalization vectors (spec 02 §3.1 Normalization, amended 2026-09-13 — audit H22). Runs on ALL THREE surfaces (core jvmTest, web vitest, extension node harness). `normalize` pins normalizeHost's OUTPUT (the A-label the engines must agree on byte-for-byte — expected values were produced by an independent oracle, WHATWG `new URL().hostname`, non-transitional UTS46); `match` pins the outcome with the REAL PSL resolver. One case per rule: IDN host, mixed case, trailing dot, www., port, userinfo, already-punycoded, decomposed (NFC), non-Latin scripts, the ß deviation (non-transitional), the Arabic-Indic digit host urimatch.json already freezes, and the empty-label reject surviving unchanged, and (R44) the U+1E9E capital sharp s REJECTED outright: lowercasing maps it to ß where UTS46 maps it to 'ss', so a saved `straẞe.de` would otherwise canonicalize to `xn--strae-oqa.de` (straße.de) — a different registrable domain from the `strasse.de` the browser reports — and fill across origins; the paired `match` case pins that it never does, beside the genuine straße.de match. Existing files stay byte-frozen: urimatch-etld1.json's `münchen.de → unknown` is a RESOLVER vector (Psl.resolve on a raw U-label) and is deliberately unchanged — canonicalization happens in normalizeHost, before the resolver ever sees the host.",
