  "limitsComment": "DNS length limits (spec 02 §3.1, amended 2026-10, security review 2026-10). NOT oracle-derived — WHATWG's non-strict host parser does not enforce them — these pin RFC 1035's rule, applied to normalizeHost's A-label output: a label longer than 63 octets or a host longer than 253 is no DNS name, so it normalizes to null and matches nothing. The rule exists to BOUND THE WORK: a co-member could otherwise plant a 300 KB label and make the punycode encoder (O(length × distinct code points)) and the PSL suffix walk (O(labels²)) freeze autofill and Health on every member's device. A run of trailing dots strips to the host in linear time (the old /\\.+$/ was quadratic).",
  "limits": [
    { "input": "https://example.com......................................../x", "expected": "example.com" },
    { "input": "https://aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.com/", "expected": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.com" },
    { "input": "https://aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.com/", "expected": null },
